+# CPS-002: DRONA Application & Experience Unification
+
+**Date:** 2026-07-20
+**Time:** 17:30 IST
+**Author:** Orion (HULK Coding Agent)
+**Repository:** batman_student
+**Status:** Draft — Awaiting Athena Approval
+
+---
+
+## 1. CPS Information
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| CPS ID | CPS-002 |
+| Title | DRONA Application & Experience Unification |
+| Date | 2026-07-20 |
+| Author | Orion (HULK Coding Agent) |
+| Repository | batman_student |
+| Status | Draft — Awaiting Athena Approval |
+
+---
+
+## 2. Business Problem
+
+CPS-001 successfully unified authentication across DRONA and Batman DD, but the two remain independent Streamlit applications.
+
+Product Owner UAT identified the following operational issues:
+
+- Multiple application launches create unnecessary complexity.
+- Separate Google authentication flows reduce usability.
+- The user perceives application boundaries between DRONA and Batman DD.
+
+The current architecture forces the user to:
+
+1. Authenticate in DRONA.
+2. Click "My Plan & Progress" to launch Batman DD in a new browser tab.
+3. Authenticate again in Batman DD (separate OAuth session).
+4. Manage two browser tabs for what should be one experience.
+
+This operational friction was identified during CPS-001 UAT and formally deferred to CPS-002.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Business Objectives
+
+| # | Objective | Rationale |
+|---|-----------|-----------|
+| 1 | DRONA shall operate as a single application. | Eliminates multi-app launch complexity. |
+| 2 | All workspaces share one authenticated session. | Eliminates re-authentication. Single `st.session_state`. |
+| 3 | Batman DD becomes the Progress Workspace within DRONA. | User never perceives historical application boundaries. |
+| 4 | "My Plan & Progress" becomes "Progress" in DRONA's sidebar. | Internal navigation replaces external link. |
+| 5 | Visual shell consistency across all workspaces. | Header, sidebar, branding, navigation, typography, spacing, and primary colors are consistent. |
+| 6 | Zero regression in existing DRONA features. | All existing functionality (Home, Learn, Super Chat, Quiz placeholder) remains unchanged. |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Scope
+
+### In Scope
+
+| # | Item | Description |
+|---|------|-------------|
+| 1 | Import Batman DD page modules into DRONA | Add imports for `render_progress_page`, `render_scheduling_page`, `render_debrief_page`, `render_notes_page` in `src/ui/app.py` |
+| 2 | Extend DRONA page routing | Add routing cases: `"PROGRESS"`, `"SCHEDULE"`, `"DEBRIEF"`, `"NOTES"` — routed via `st.session_state.page` |
+| 3 | Update DRONA sidebar navigation | Replace external "My Plan & Progress" HTML link with internal `st.button("📈 Progress")`; add Schedule, Daily Debrief, Quick Notes buttons |
+| 4 | Remove external Batman DD launch URL | Delete `href="http://localhost:8501" target="_blank"` inline HTML from sidebar |
+| 5 | Deprecate `src/batman_dd/app.py` | Batman DD ceases as an independent application entry point |
+| 6 | Apply DRONA shell to all workspaces | All workspaces render within DRONA's existing `st.set_page_config`, sidebar, header, and footer |
+| 7 | Preserve all existing DRONA session state | `learn_messages`, `superchat_messages`, `page`, `subject`, `student_id` continue working unchanged |
+| 8 | Produce Implementation Report | Per HCA Playbook standard |
+| 9 | Produce Implementation Change Log | Per Athena review requirement |
+| 10 | Produce UAT Package | Per HCA Playbook standard |
+
+### Out of Scope
+
+| # | Item | Reason |
+|---|------|--------|
+| 1 | CSS consolidation | Deferred to future CPS. Workspace-specific DD components retain existing styling. DRONA shell elements remain consistent. |
+| 2 | File relocation of Batman DD modules | Pages remain at `src/batman_dd/pages/`. Zero refactoring risk. |
+| 3 | Deletion of `src/batman_dd/` directory | Preserves history and import paths. Cleanup deferred. |
+| 4 | Business logic changes | All existing services (`student_progress_service.py`, `student_schedule_service.py`, `student_notes_service.py`) remain unchanged. |
+| 5 | Data migration | Student data at `data/students/` remains unchanged. |
+| 6 | Infrastructure changes | No Docker, CI/CD, or deployment changes. |
+| 7 | Authentication changes | `auth_gate.py` remains as-is. CPS-001 auth implementation is reused. |
+| 8 | Configuration changes | `settings.py`, `secrets/`, `.env` unchanged. |
+| 9 | New features | No new business functionality in CPS-002. Unification only. |
+| 10 | Quiz implementation | "Quiz (Coming Soon)" remains a disabled placeholder. |
+| 11 | Branch rename | CPS-001 branch name conventions are historical. CPS-002 uses `orion/` namespace per AGENT_BRANCHING_STANDARD. |
