+## 7a. Implementation Principles
+
+| # | Principle | Rationale |
+|---|-----------|-----------|
+| 1 | Modify the minimum amount of code necessary. | Reduces regression risk. Single file (`src/ui/app.py`) modification target. |
+| 2 | Prefer reuse over duplication. | Batman DD page modules are imported, not rewritten. |
+| 3 | Existing business logic shall remain unchanged. | All services (`student_progress_service.py`, `student_schedule_service.py`, `student_notes_service.py`) are reused as-is. |
+| 4 | Existing data structures shall remain unchanged. | No data migration. Student data, curriculum data, notes, schedules untouched. |
+| 5 | Workspace integration shall occur through composition rather than relocation. | Pages stay at `src/batman_dd/pages/`. DRONA imports and composes them. |
+| 6 | DRONA remains the only executable application. | `streamlit run src/ui/app.py` is the sole entry point. |
+| 7 | Batman DD modules become reusable implementation modules. | `src/batman_dd/` provides importable renderers and services, not a standalone app. |
+| 8 | Architectural decisions are outside implementation scope and must be referred to Athena. | Any deviation from the approved Architecture Review must be escalated. |
